0009 — classlink.rs: inheritance diagnostics found by the magic-methods pass
(apply on top of 0001-0008).

* do_inherit_property for static redeclarations: a static property
  redeclaring an inherited non-static one fails with "Cannot redeclare non
  static %s::$%s as static %s::$%s"; redeclaring an inherited static one with
  narrower visibility fails with "Access level to %s::$%s must be %s (as in
  class %s)%s" (the 9 tests/classes/property_override_*Static* tests).
* do_inherit_constant_check: a redeclared class constant may only widen
  visibility: "Access level to %s::%s must be %s (as in class|interface
  %s)%s" (tests/classes/constants_visibility_error_003, _004).
* do_inheritance_check_on_method: private methods are skipped only when
  they are neither abstract nor the constructor, so a final private
  constructor still cannot be overridden (tests/classes/final_private_ctor);
  a constructor is checked against its abstract/interface prototype and the
  access error names the prototype's class (Zend/tests/magic_methods/
  bug61970_2: "must be public (as in class Foo)").
* Bug #81582: a __toString() taken from an (already declared) trait also
  makes the class implement Stringable (Zend/tests/magic_methods/
  stringable_trait).
* interface_gets_implemented hooks run before the abstract-method check, as
  do_implement_interface runs before zend_verify_abstract_class. Needed for
  tests/classes/bug65768 once ext/date registers its DateTimeInterface hook
  ("DateTimeInterface can't be implemented by user classes"; php-ext-date
  does not register one yet).

